<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST - S-E-Banken sees Swedish '97 GDP 2.1 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - S-E-Banken sees Swedish '97 GDP 2.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial Swedish bank S-E-Banken issued the following forecasts for the Swedish economy on Tuesday.</p>
<p> (pct change unless otherwise stated)  1997	1998</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product (GDP)	     2.1	 2.5</p>
<p> Private consumption			  1.5	 1.9</p>
<p> Public consumption			  -0.8	 0.5</p>
<p> Investments				    2.6	 4.0</p>
<p> Exports					  6.1	 5.0</p>
<p> Imports					  5.0	 4.0</p>
<p> CPI, annual average			  0.8	 2.0</p>
<p> Industrial production			3.5	 4.5</p>
<p>Unemployment, excluding people in</p>
<p> government work schemes		    7.5	 6.3</p>
<p> Trade Balance (billion Skr)		130	 145</p>
<p> Current account (billion Skr)	   51.0	65.5</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
